  "note": "EM runs over the enumerated derivation trees of each sentence: a tree is weighted by its probability under the current model, and the M-step is add-one smoothing, so the fit is MAP under a Dirichlet prior and its objective, which includes that prior, never decreases. The even-split model is the start of EM and the model of v1. The uniform PCFG is improper by Booth and Thompson: the lower bound on the spectral radius of its mean-count matrix is above 1 and every nonterminal reachable from the start symbol is productive, so its perplexity is a score under a deficient model and not a baseline at all. The bounds are computed in f64 without interval arithmetic; the uniform bound is far above 1 compared with the rounding error. This is still a demonstration on a few dozen sentences per mode, not a language model.",
